{
  "about": "The controller and the checkout service each test their real code against a byte-for-byte copy of this file: sparkwing internal/controller/testdata and sparkwing-platform internal/billing/testdata. Change both copies together. Each route's request is the whole body the controller sends with the bearer token; each response is the service's whole answer. refund_event is the captured Stripe test-mode refund.created event, with an event-level livemode and no object-level livemode. refill_cases are the service's answers to each Stripe outcome of the refill request. refusals are answers the controller must classify: final ones are about the request and close the refill or refund for the owners and operator; the others, outages and a misconfigured pairing (wrong token, route or deployment), are retried with backoff.",
